    turnFlow: "One banker and multiple players. Each receives five cards. Players split their five cards into a three-card set (total must be a multiple of 10) and a two-card hand. The two-card hand's point value (units digit only, e.g. 17 counts as 7) is the hand rank. Banker does the same. Compare each player's hand to the banker: higher point value wins. Niu Niu (both three- and two-card parts total zero) is the highest normal hand. Ties broken by highest single card. Equal bet pays 1:1 (minus 5% commission on wins); Double bet pays 1:1 for 1-6 points, 2:1 for 7-9, 3:1 for Niu Niu (player can lose up to 3x on Double).",
